WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.481
- What is happening?

00:00:01.481 --> 00:00:02.880
This could be the worst medical show

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.300
in the history of medical shows.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.930
I heard there's a new medical drama

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.350
floating around on YouTube
called Attaway General.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.062
I'm ready for a cringe-worthy
YouTube medical show.

00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:14.550
- As first-year TBs, you
guys will be on pediatrics.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.640
You'll help with clerical work, transpo,

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.569
keeping patients company.

00:00:17.569 --> 00:00:18.690
- Yes.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.250
- Babysitting, great.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.140
- That's right, Georgia.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.861
- This feels like the exact same intro

00:00:23.861 --> 00:00:26.430
that I think Grey's Anatomy started when

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.260
we did our first Grey's Anatomy review.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.200
It feels like a little
hazing is happening here,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.220
and we don't haze our
volunteers in the hospital.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.770
- Ambulance bay needs hands.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:34.979
Paging Dr. Henry and everyone on call.

00:00:34.979 --> 00:00:37.560
Metro bus crash downtown.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.980
We're about to be at capacity.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.910
- Somewhat similar.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.130
It does happen in the hospital.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:41.976
We have a triage nurse.

00:00:41.976 --> 00:00:45.470
For example, if I have a
patient in my outpatient center

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.940
that I need to be seen
in the ER, I call ahead.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.830
The nurse triage is in,
gets a doctor ready.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:52.920
If we need a trauma bay,
they get that ready.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:53.830
All the equipment.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:54.810
You want to be prepared.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.700
- This is Mae.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.740
She's our top second-year.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.760
She's gonna finish the
tour, while I go home.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.630
I'll be back when I can.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.380
- I also didn't know that volunteers have

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.850
years of seniority like residents have,

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.330
that first-year, second-year, third-year,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.000
fourth-year, and they have seniority

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.833
over each other.

00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:12.097
I feel like this show is grooming teens

00:01:12.097 --> 00:01:15.328
to become hardcore fans of Grey's Anatomy.

00:01:15.328 --> 00:01:18.210
(dramatic music)

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.810
What were those chest compressions?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:20.670
What is this?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.738
You gotta use the full
weight of your body.

00:01:22.738 --> 00:01:24.343
- Oh, this is gonna suck.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.470
- This is gonna be amazing.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:27.303
- I'm not gonna lie.

00:01:27.303 --> 00:01:30.299
The person who's there on the
first day of introductions,

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:32.170
and they're taking notes,

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.870
I was always super
intimidated by that person.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.220
Should I be taking notes?

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.390
Am I missing something?

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.050
What if they're gonna
know something I don't,

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.570
and then I realize sometimes
you need to take notes,

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.951
and sometimes you just need to be there,

00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:44.860
present as a human.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.454
- There's a lunch tray
in here for everyone.

00:01:46.454 --> 00:01:48.908
Make sure everyone eats at least half

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.230
before you leave.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.990
- What happened to a proper orientation,

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.100
teaching them how to use safety equipment,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.272
knowing when to notify senior staff,

00:01:56.272 --> 00:01:58.680
putting on gloves and gowns?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.010
These things need to be taught,

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.310
and I hope they were checked
for their immunizations

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.010
because the last thing
we want is our volunteers

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.390
spreading illness throughout the hospital.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.478
- Why did you volunteer
to work at a hospital?

00:02:07.478 --> 00:02:11.393
- I got arrested, beats juvie.

00:02:13.721 --> 00:02:14.710
(upbeat music)

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:18.530
- Do not blow into a glove with your mouth

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.670
before you put it in.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.850
A, it's not really hygienic

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.790
because you have a lot of
bacteria in your mouth,

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.720
but number two, there's humidity
that comes from your mouth,

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.680
and have you ever tried to put your hand

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:29.513
into a wet, moist glove?

00:02:29.513 --> 00:02:30.346
Ugh, and it's hard.

00:02:30.346 --> 00:02:32.898
(upbeat music)

00:02:34.881 --> 00:02:37.200
Fun fact, those beds are accurate.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.960
They're legit, and they're
insanely expensive.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.220
ICU beds are 25 to $30,000 each.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.830
I've seen those go even
higher, and medical beds,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:47.860
which are just the plain ones,

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.530
are five to 10,000 a bed.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.095
Imagine a 300-bed hospital.

00:02:51.095 --> 00:02:52.470
It's a lot of moolah.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:53.303
- I'm a little worried right now

00:02:53.303 --> 00:02:54.960
because I'm losing a lot of blood,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.100
and my favorite sweatshirt.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.820
- You should be fine to wait a little.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.710
If you hit an artery, you
would have passed out by now.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:04.410
- Oh, we have pre-med students up in here.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.000
She's like, if you hit an artery,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.310
you wouldn't be here right now.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.050
Yes, but why in the world
is she making contact

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.870
with a patient and giving medical advice?

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.790
Huge no-no to our volunteers.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:14.623
Can you be there?

00:03:14.623 --> 00:03:15.680
Can you help them out?

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:16.513
Can you do all these things?

00:03:16.513 --> 00:03:19.069
Yes, but you're not trained
to give medical care

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:22.290
no matter how many of my
YouTube videos you watch.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.520
- Six-year-old female, third-degree burns,

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.970
possible smoke inhalation.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.820
We couldn't get a line in.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.360
- Give me a 24-needle norepinephrine.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:30.220
- What else can I do?

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.360
- Oh, you've done more than enough.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.990
You can go back to your normal duties.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:33.823
- Okay.

00:03:33.823 --> 00:03:34.680
- [Nurse] She's close to coding.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.220
- [Doctor] Come on, show me a vein.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.930
- None of this is medically accurate.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.330
She's close to coding, what?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.550
If a patient's not breathing,
that means they're coding.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:44.540
That means they're dead,

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.950
and you need to bring them back to life,

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.990
and that means you need
to do chest compressions,

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.560
chest compressions, chest compressions,

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.790
and this doctor asking
for a 24-gauge needle?

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.750
I don't even understand
what he's hoping to do here.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.900
If he's starting to try to start an IV,

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.950
you don't start an IV
with a 24-gauge needle.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.650
You start with an 18-gauge needle,

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:00.850
which is much wider.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.251
None of this makes sense.

00:04:02.251 --> 00:04:03.478
(dramatic music)

00:04:03.478 --> 00:04:04.480
(hospital equipment beeps)

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:07.890
I love that the doctor, while
he's reaching for the syringe,

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:08.723
he's reaching for it,

00:04:08.723 --> 00:04:10.216
and he's still tapping on her elbow.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.270
What are you doing my man?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.360
What do you tapping him for?

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.340
What are you trying to find?

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.840
- What did you do to get arrested?

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.740
- In prison, you're never
supposed to ask about the crime.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:23.580
Come on, dude.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.560
You're the last one.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.880
You have to eat.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.140
Hey, don't ignore me.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:30.196
- Hey Jack, maybe try a gentler approach.

00:04:30.196 --> 00:04:31.056
(Mikhail laughs)

00:04:31.056 --> 00:04:32.770
- Oh God, this is so
awkward, it's cringe-y.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.780
Hey, why don't you try a gentler approach.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.899
- Stevie, sweetie, you need to eat

00:04:35.899 --> 00:04:39.000
to get big and strong and feel better.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.420
- No.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.890
- It's actually really good.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.220
Let me show you, mmm.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.457
- Did she really take
a bite off the spoon,

00:04:47.457 --> 00:04:49.890
and then she is giving the same spoon

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.843
to the child?

00:04:56.905 --> 00:04:58.195
Oh, I love that my man
is just standing there

00:04:58.195 --> 00:05:00.370
in a shearling jacket.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:01.300
Maybe take it off.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.740
Make yourself like you're at work.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.476
Put on a uniform, not a fancy jacket

00:05:04.476 --> 00:05:06.836
like you're part of an after-school play

00:05:06.836 --> 00:05:08.550
for The Lost Boys.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.489
- What are you doing?

00:05:09.489 --> 00:05:10.322
- Whoa.

00:05:10.322 --> 00:05:11.155
- [Woman] Don't come any closer.

00:05:11.155 --> 00:05:12.327
- I don't think that's gonna hurt anyone.

00:05:12.327 --> 00:05:14.515
- Depends where I put it.

00:05:14.515 --> 00:05:15.855
(Mikhail laughs)

00:05:15.855 --> 00:05:18.460
(hospital equipment beeps)

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:22.070
- The cardiac rhythm behind
them is the scariest rhythm

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.250
ever, and there's 10 of them?

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.380
Go figure why, in different colors.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.990
They were like, let's just
put them all on the screen

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:28.823
because they're colorful.

00:05:28.823 --> 00:05:29.813
- Squeeze as tight as you can.

00:05:29.813 --> 00:05:31.556
Now, don't worry about hurting her.

00:05:31.556 --> 00:05:32.389
(hospital equipment beeps)

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:33.222
- Why does-

00:05:33.222 --> 00:05:34.432
- And we're in.

00:05:34.432 --> 00:05:35.943
(hospital equipment beeps)

00:05:35.943 --> 00:05:37.363
- What is he doing?

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.633
This is just insanity.

00:05:39.633 --> 00:05:41.500
(hospital equipment beeps)

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.450
- Keep up the rescue breaths.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.004
- Nothing changed on the screen.

00:05:44.004 --> 00:05:45.770
What is happening?

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.100
This could be the worst medical show

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.890
in the history of medical shows.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.840
Doc McStuffins was more accurate.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:52.964
Bus boy, why are you back here?

00:05:52.964 --> 00:05:54.811
- Just waiting to get my stitches removed.

00:05:54.811 --> 00:05:56.590
- Mind if I take a look?

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.070
- Two problems here.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:01.170
One, why in the world do
you go to the emergency room

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.320
to get your stitches removed?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.400
You could go to your primary
care doctor's office,

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.310
and save a huge ER bill,
and a wait in the ER.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:09.650
Two, why is the volunteer taking a look

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.700
at anything medical.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.890
That is not ethical.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:12.723
It's wrong.

00:06:12.723 --> 00:06:14.144
- Sutures look like they healed nicely.

00:06:14.144 --> 00:06:15.600
Shouldn't have too much of a scar.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.660
- This is what people must
think happens in hospitals.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.210
The writer was, I wonder
what volunteers do?

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.740
They must help with patients.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.000
No, they don't.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.146
Can you imagine someone
with zero medical experience

00:06:26.146 --> 00:06:27.973
giving out medical advice?

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.170
Oh wait, that's like
Gwyneth Paltrow and Goop.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.093
I guess it does happen.

00:06:32.093 --> 00:06:33.760
- [Both] Damn!

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.550
- Nurse Sandy told me to be careful.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.160
One of the boys bullied the other,

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.932
and is pretty dangerous.

00:06:38.932 --> 00:06:40.500
- Oh, bullies are scary.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.500
- I've never seen a medical uniform

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.610
specify the age of the person wearing it.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:49.410
It doesn't say medical volunteer,
it says teen volunteer.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:51.476
Who needs to know that information?

00:06:51.476 --> 00:06:52.309
- Where are you headed?

00:06:52.309 --> 00:06:56.535
- I was on my way to the
supply room for supplies.

00:06:56.535 --> 00:06:59.353
- That's funny, so was I.

00:07:00.845 --> 00:07:02.063
(Mikhail laughs)

00:07:02.063 --> 00:07:03.660
- [Woman] I didn't know you
were Dr. Henry's protege.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:08.160
- I didn't know that volunteers
were considered proteges.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.920
I used to think that would
be a role for residents

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.870
or med students, nurses.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.490
- [Man] Smart is the new sexy.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.815
I read that somewhere.

00:07:15.815 --> 00:07:16.880
(Mikhail laughs)

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.480
Cringe.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.313
Cringe.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.430
I appreciate it, though.

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.370
I like people representing smart folks.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:24.846
The fact that he said he read it somewhere

00:07:24.846 --> 00:07:26.920
means he reads.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.210
- I'm so sorry you're hurting.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.888
How about an ice pack for that eye?

00:07:29.888 --> 00:07:31.440
- No I'm good.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.350
- Can I get you some pudding, juice?

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.580
- You know what's really important?

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.900
Whenever a patient is
admitted into a hospital,

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.330
or coming into the emergency room,

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.427
there are certain orders
that we place as doctors

00:07:40.427 --> 00:07:42.950
whether or not a patient
is allowed to eat,

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.860
and what diet they have to follow

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.480
because some patients have
trouble swallowing certain foods.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.560
Some patients should be NPO,
which means nothing by mouth

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.040
because they're going for a procedure,

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.990
or, perhaps, a surgery, so
the fact that these kids

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.230
are running around the hospital
and offering people food,

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:59.320
while it is nice, in theory,
that's not their job,

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.009
and they need to be really
careful who they're feeding

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:03.127
because if someone is going for a surgery

00:08:03.127 --> 00:08:05.818
in an hour, and they give them a sandwich,

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.800
that's a problem because the surgery's

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.800
gonna get canceled.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.310
- You know I've never been in a fight?

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:11.760
Maybe you can give me some pointers.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.690
- I'm not sure this device that he has

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.200
on his head, I've never seen it before.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.240
I honestly don't think
it's a medical device,

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.010
but because I haven't seen
it, and because I'm not

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.200
technically a trauma surgeon,
I'm not gonna comment on it.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.180
It looks shady though.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.593
- [Man] You really don't
know where the bandages are?

00:08:26.449 --> 00:08:27.410
- [Woman] No, I do, I
just needed an excuse

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.870
to get you in here.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:31.620
(romantic music)

00:08:33.151 --> 00:08:33.984
- [Man] You don't even.

00:08:33.984 --> 00:08:36.170
- If you hadn't snitched, I'd
still be on the lacrosse team.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:37.682
I should've kicked you harder.

00:08:37.682 --> 00:08:39.153
- Hey, enough.

00:08:39.153 --> 00:08:40.420
What is it with you kids?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.230
You can't follow the
simplest instructions.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.992
- I love that all the medical dramas

00:08:43.992 --> 00:08:47.400
are all doctors doing everything,
transporting patients,

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.013
ordering tests, performing the surgeries,

00:08:49.013 --> 00:08:51.260
talking to the patients,
everything is them,

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.052
and in this show, the
volunteers are the only ones.

00:08:54.052 --> 00:08:55.650
They're treating the patients,

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:56.980
they're breaking up the fights,

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:58.700
they're making out in the hallways.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.440
What is going on?

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.320
Include other characters.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.930
Health care is a collaboration.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.801
- You're supposed to
protect your patient, Kit.

00:09:05.801 --> 00:09:08.280
- What are they, police officers?

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.910
You're supposed to protect and serve

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:10.790
as a volunteer.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.860
- Can you tell me what happened to Holden?

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:13.854
- No updates, Kit.

00:09:13.854 --> 00:09:16.437
(solemn music)

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.250
Holden has a severe heart condition.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:30.670
- We don't give patient information out

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.480
to volunteers just because
they have crushes on them.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.890
Patient information is a protected entity.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.130
Oh my God, for a chocolate bar?

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.680
- Is he gonna be okay?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.510
- It's not a good prognosis,

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:45.000
but he's at Attaway General,
getting the best care there is.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.370
- I may have to disagree with
you on that little point.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:51.660
In fact, probably more
like Attaway Funeral Home,

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:53.924
as opposed to Attaway General Hospital.

00:09:53.924 --> 00:09:55.040
Just saying.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.310
Here's a higher quality
medical show, Doc McStuffins.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:00.960
Yes, it's a cartoon about a preschooler.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:01.960
If you want someone a little older,

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.870
check out my man Dougie Houser here,

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.200
Neil Patrick Harris, NPH.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.120
Which one you clicking?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.734
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:10:09.734 --> 00:10:12.317
(upbeat music)

